{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-4-2","title":"prop:dc-ch3-4-2","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":1394,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#prop:dc-ch3-4-2","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-maxdeduction]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speedchart]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velbound]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior-minimizing]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-gramsmall]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-invdiagonal]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-pairsmall]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velsmall]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-length]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-edist]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-join-metric]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-endpoint-id]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-competitor-lb]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-eqon-flow-reading]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-uniqueness-engine]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch3-4-2","line":3636,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[convex neighborhoods]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-4-2}\n\n  \\uses{thm:dc-ch3-3-7, lem:dc-ch3-4-1, lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-maxdeduction, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speedchart, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velbound, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior-minimizing, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-gramsmall, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-invdiagonal, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-pairsmall, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velsmall, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-length, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-edist, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-join-metric, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-endpoint-id, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-competitor-lb, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-eqon-flow-reading, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-uniqueness-engine, def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.2}\n  For any $p\\in M$ there exists $\\beta>0$ such that the closed geodesic ball $\\overline{B_\\beta(p)}$ is\n  strongly convex (\\cref{def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex}). (The closed ball is used deliberately: the\n  literal open-ball form is unsatisfiable at a boundary diagonal, see below.)\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  Let $c$ be as in \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1}. Choose $\\delta>0$ and $W$ as in \\cref{thm:dc-ch3-3-7}\n  with $\\delta<\\frac{c}{2}$, and take $\\beta<\\delta$ with $\\overline{B_\\beta(p)}\\subset W$. Let\n  $q_1,q_2\\in\\overline{B_\\beta(p)}$ and let $\\gamma$ be the unique geodesic of length\n  $<2\\delta<c$ joining them; then $\\gamma\\subset B_c(p)$. If the interior of\n  $\\gamma$ is not contained in $B_\\beta(p)$, there is an interior point $m$ where the\n  maximum distance $r$ from $p$ to $\\gamma$ is attained; near $m$ the points of\n  $\\gamma$ remain in $\\overline{B_r(p)}$. Since $m\\in B_c(p)$ this contradicts\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict}: at $m$ the tangency $\\partial F/\\partial t(0)=0$ holds\n  (Gauss lemma) and the strict separation $F(0)<F(s)$ for $s\\neq0$ forces points of\n  $\\gamma$ near $m$ \\emph{strictly} outside $\\overline{B_r(p)}$, contradicting the\n  maximum. Hence the interior of $\\gamma$ lies in $B_\\beta(p)$, proving the proposition.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[convex neighborhoods] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d342d32\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23thm%3Adc-ch3-3-7\">↗ thm:dc-ch3-3-7</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-strict\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-rebase\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-window\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-nomax\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-bridge\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-maxdeduction\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-maxdeduction</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-speedchart\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speedchart</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-velbound\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velbound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-interior\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-interior-minimizing\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-interior-minimizing</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-gramsmall\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-gramsmall</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-invdiagonal\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-invdiagonal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-pairsmall\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-pairsmall</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-velsmall\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-velsmall</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-segment-length\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-length</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-segment-edist\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-segment-edist</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-join-metric\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-join-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-endpoint-id\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-endpoint-id</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-competitor-lb\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-competitor-lb</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-eqon-flow-reading\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-eqon-flow-reading</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-uniqueness-engine\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-uniqueness-engine</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex\">↗ def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:4.2</span></span>For any <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> there exists <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta &gt;0$\">$\\beta &gt;0$</span> such that the closed geodesic ball <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$\">$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$</span> is strongly convex (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368332d342d322d7374726f6e676c79636f6e766578\">section 3</a>). (The closed ball is used deliberately: the literal open-ball form is unsatisfiable at a boundary diagonal, see below.)  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> be as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d31\">section 3</a>. Choose <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\delta &gt;0$\">$\\delta &gt;0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23thm%3Adc-ch3-3-7\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a64632d6368332d332d37\">item 5</a> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\delta &lt;\\frac{c}{2}$\">$\\delta &lt;\\frac{c}{2}$</span>, and take <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta &lt;\\delta $\">$\\beta &lt;\\delta $</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}\\subset W$\">$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}\\subset W$</span>. Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_1,q_2\\in \\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$\">$q_1,q_2\\in \\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> be the unique geodesic of length <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$&lt;2\\delta &lt;c$\">$&lt;2\\delta &lt;c$</span> joining them; then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma \\subset B_c(p)$\">$\\gamma \\subset B_c(p)$</span>. If the interior of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> is not contained in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\beta (p)$\">$B_\\beta (p)$</span>, there is an interior point <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m$\">$m$</span> where the maximum distance <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r$\">$r$</span> from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> is attained; near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m$\">$m$</span> the points of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> remain in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\overline{B_r(p)}$\">$\\overline{B_r(p)}$</span>. Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m\\in B_c(p)$\">$m\\in B_c(p)$</span> this contradicts <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-1-strict\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d312d737472696374\">section 3</a>: at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m$\">$m$</span> the tangency <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\partial F/\\partial t(0)=0$\">$\\partial F/\\partial t(0)=0$</span> holds (Gauss lemma) and the strict separation <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F(0)&lt;F(s)$\">$F(0)&lt;F(s)$</span> for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s\\neq 0$\">$s\\neq 0$</span> forces points of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m$\">$m$</span> <em>strictly</em> outside <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\overline{B_r(p)}$\">$\\overline{B_r(p)}$</span>, contradicting the maximum. Hence the interior of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> lies in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\beta (p)$\">$B_\\beta (p)$</span>, proving the proposition. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-3-1-piecewise-transport","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7","title":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7","label":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-1-strict"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-rebase"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-window"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-nomax"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball","label":"l